$$\begin{aligned}
\cos 2x &= \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\
\Leftrightarrow\ 2\cos^2 x - 1 &= \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\
\Leftrightarrow\ 2\cos^2 x &= \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} + 1 \\
\Leftrightarrow\ \cos^2 x &= \frac{\sqrt{2}}{4} + \frac{1}{2} \\
\Leftrightarrow\ \cos x &= \pm\sqrt{\frac{\sqrt{2}}{4} + \frac{2}{4}} 
= \pm\sqrt{\frac{\sqrt{2} + 2}{4}} 
= \pm\frac{\sqrt{\sqrt{2} + 2}}{2}
\end{aligned}$$

Koska $\frac{\pi}{2} \le x \le \pi$, niin $\cos x = -\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{2 + \sqrt{2}}$.

